#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "provisioning.license.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki To Provisioning License API Okta Authentication
	Testing Okta Authentication permission for users

Scenario: View license with okta authentication using a valid user
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to view licenses  a license form options with the okta ID Session

	When I log into the dev domain as "koconnell@xtivia.com.broken" with password "wqd@NUX2jwv@bhp@gnz1"
	And I obtain the okta session ID value from the dev domain page
	Then I should be able to view the license on the account "Xtivia, Inc." with the name "Test1" using the okta session id value "${staticOktaSessionId}"
	And I should be able to view the following generate license form options for the account "Xtivia, Inc." with the product group "DXP" using the okta session id value "${staticOktaSessionId}"
	| Label | 7.0 |
	| Label | 7.1 |
	| Label | 7.2 |
	| Label | 7.3 |
	| Label | 7.4 |

Scenario: View license with okta authentication using second valid user
	Testing the ability to view a license form options with the okta ID Session

	When I log into the dev domain as "vamshi@xtivia.com.broken" with password "wqd@NUX2jwv@bhp@gnz1"
	And I obtain the okta session ID value from the dev domain page
	Then I should be able to view the license on the account "Xtivia, Inc." with the name "Test1" using the okta session id value "${staticOktaSessionId}"
	And I should be able to view the following generate license form options for the account "Xtivia, Inc." with the product group "DXP" using the okta session id value "${staticOktaSessionId}"
	| Label | 7.0 |
	| Label | 7.1 |
	| Label | 7.2 |
	| Label | 7.3 |
	| Label | 7.4 |

Scenario: View license with okta authentication attempt using a non permissioned user
	Testing the ability to not view a license form options  with the okta ID Session

	When I log into the dev domain as "mohamed.othman@liferay.com.broken" with password "wqd@NUX2jwv@bhp@gnz1"
	And I obtain the okta session ID value from the dev domain page
	Then I should not be able to view the license on the account "Xtivia, Inc." with the name "Test1" using the okta session id value "${staticOktaSessionId}"